# TAB UI (Edit Page)

## Scope
  This prompt contains only TAB UI requirements for the editing page.

## Layout
  - Show scenario tabs at the top-left of edit toolbar.
  - Move edit action buttons to the top-right.
  - Tabs must look like file tabs (not normal action buttons).
  - Tabs must be smaller than action buttons and use clearly different colors.
  - Tab title area and close `x` area should look like one connected tab.
  - Scenario name input is removed from the toolbar.
    It is now inside the Save Scenario dialog (see Save flow).

## Behavior
  - Each tab represents one scenario editing context.
  - Switching tab changes active scenario/workspace.
    The current workspace state (blocks, startPlay IDs, scenario guard, errors)
    is serialized into the tab before switching, and restored when switching back.
  - First tab has no close button.
  - Tabs after the first have close button `x`.
  - Closing active tab switches to a neighbor tab (prefer previous).
  - First tab (index 0) cannot be closed.
  - If current tab is an unsaved new tab (no original name), Create/Edit reuses it.
    Otherwise a new tab is opened.
  - When Edit is clicked for a scenario already open in a tab, switch to that tab.

## Open by block double-click
  - If user double-clicks a Scenario block in workspace,
    open that scenario in a new tab.
  - If the scenario is already open in an existing tab, switch to that tab instead.
  - Double-click is detected as two click events on the same block within 500ms.

## Save flow
  - Clicking `Save Scenario` opens save-name dialog with:
    - Scenario Name input (pre-filled with current tab's saved name, or empty for new).
    - `Confirm` button saves the scenario.
    - `Cancel` button closes the dialog without saving.
  - Pressing `Enter` in the name input confirms save (same as clicking `Confirm`).
  - Pressing `Escape` cancels and closes the dialog.
  - Clicking outside the dialog card closes the dialog without saving.
  - On confirm, save active tab scenario.
  - Tab title should update with saved scenario name.

## Tab state per tab
  Each tab stores the following state independently:
  - Blockly workspace JSON (serialized on tab switch or save)
  - Original scenario name (set when scenario is opened or saved)
  - Tab label (display name shown in tab, mirrors original name or 'New Scenario')
  - startPlay ID counter state (startPlayNextId, startPlayAssignedIds)
  - Scenario guard disabled names set
  - Error list items

## Visibility
  - Tab UI is visible only in edit page.
  - JSON/Tree modals are not part of this prompt scope.
